Computes the new properties: transform/translate added up, opacity, clip-path,
clip (only for absolute and fixed boxes, as CSS has it), row-gap and
column-gap, the grid properties as tokens; display: grid becomes flex
with m_grid set, so litehtml does for a grid all it does for flex but
the layout. An element with a mask-image has the mask drawn as its
background, its address marked "mask:#rrggbb:" with the background
colour, which the browser draws the mask's shape in: icons are made so.
And an absolutely positioned or floated inline-flex box becomes flex, as
CSS has it: Wikipedia's hidden checkboxes took a line's room each.

